    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Doran Estates are delighted to present No. 51 Walkinstown Parade to the market. This attractive two-storey, three-bedroom home offers over 100 sq.m. of accommodation, including an extended ground floor which provides valuable additional living space.\r\nWhile the property would benefit from refurbishment, it offers an excellent opportunity for a new owner to put their own stamp on the home and unlock its full potential.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming porch leading into a bright entrance hallway. To the front is a well-proportioned living room with a feature fireplace. Double doors lead through to a separate sitting room, which can also be accessed directly from the hallway. The sitting room benefits from useful storage, while an internal window overlooking the kitchen allows additional natural light into the space.\r\nTo the rear is the kitchen and dining area, with access to a practical utility room. The utility room provides access to the downstairs bathroom and the rear garden, which offers a pleasant outdoor space and a great spot to enjoy the longer summer evenings.\r\nUpstairs, there are two generous double bedrooms, one positioned to the front and the other to the rear, together with a single bedroom also located to the rear. The accommodation is well laid out and offers plenty of scope for improvement and modernisation.\r\n\r\nThe location is a major attraction, with Walkinstown Parade close to a wide range of local amenities including shops, schools, parks and sporting facilities. The Red Luas line is approximately a ten-minute walk away, while there are excellent bus connections to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The M50 and N7 are both less than a five-minute drive from the property, providing convenient access to Dublin and the wider region.\r\nNo. 51 Walkinstown Parade is a property with genuine potential, offering generous accommodation, useful additional ground-floor space and a well-connected location. With the right vision and refurbishment, this home could be transformed into a fantastic property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hallway: \r\nWelcoming entrance hallway \r\nLiving Room: (4.10m x 3.20m)\r\nLiving Room with fireplace, with access to a sitting room\r\nSitting Room: (4.90m x 2.80m)\r\nSitting Room with storage, with access to a kitchen\r\nKitchen / Diner: (5.00m x 3.00m)\r\nKitchen / Diner with access to a Utility Room\r\nUtility Room: (2.80m x 1.90m)\r\nUtility Room with access to a Bathroom and back garden\r\nBathroom: (2.70m x 1.70m)\r\nBathroom with tiled floor and tiled walls, shower, whb, WC. , extractor fan.\r\nBedroom 1: (4.00m x 3.00m)\r\nDouble bedroom with storage, located to the front of the house\r\nBedroom 2: (3.90m x 2.70m)\r\nDouble bedroom, located to the back of the house\r\nBedroom 3: (2.80m x 2.40m)\r\nSingle bedroom, located to the back of the house\r\nOutside: (approx. 11.00m x 4.90m)\r\nBack Garden\r\n \r\nPlease note that Doran Estates have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services and cannot verify their working condition or provide any warranty in relation thereto. Interested parties are strongly advised to carry out their own inspections and satisfy themselves regarding the condition and functionality of all items prior to the completion of the sale. Floor plans are provided for illustrative purposes only; all measurements are approximate and may not be to scale. Photographs are for guidance only and may not represent the current state of the property. Doran Estates would recommend that all purchaser carry out a full and detailed inspection of the property themselves as well as engaging a surveyor to carryout an inspection on their behalf."
